#530 closing pass 4 -- table 2 predictions (panel cells + lane questions), written BEFORE any table-2 log.

L3gate  -> 111/111 ESCAPE.  Lane-3 stores in the probe land on SCR 0x3ff (inert read) and split heads on 0x3ff / 0x5f
           (unmapped); wdc 0x1f7 is NOT PRESENT on the probe's machine (bus_isa.c adds wdc only when an IDE disk image
           exists).  Guest-visible: disc E at 0x63 (the 8042 PC-style stub's static toggle) -- store flip 0x0 -> 0x10.
WT6     -> 111/111 ESCAPE (tailw's 0x60 tails find an EMPTY queue; heads of len 6 at SCR inert).  Disc C: tail 6 DIB 1 -> 0.
WTsplit -> 111/111 ESCAPE (same reason, widths 3,5,6,7).  Disc C: tails 6, 5, 3 and 7 all DIB 1 -> 0.
R2w     -> 111/111 ESCAPE (`iir lca rd' is (1,2) only; every other lane-2 lca read is MSR 0x3fe, inert).
           Disc B: LDWU/LDL/LDQ SP(0x3fa) lane & 3: 0x2 -> 0x1.
R2w2    -> 111/111 ESCAPE.  Disc B: LDWU 0x2 -> 0x1, LDL/LDQ unchanged.
RD2L0   -> 111/111 ESCAPE (every lca read of 0x60 in the probe has ONE reply queued; a second read of an empty queue
           returns last_scancode, the same 0x55).  Disc D: DIB after 1 -> 0 at LDBU (1,0), LDQ (8,0) and the LDQ tail 6.
Discriminator on the table-1 legs: dataA  A: 0x2 -> 0x1 on both nonzero stores;  L1gate  E tog61 store flip 0x10,
           F pit41 0x34/hi -> hi/0x34, G cmos71 0x40 -> 0x0;  Wpure: A, C (all tails), E (all four ports) differ.
